+# Actual ProcessRuntime poll lifecycle observer1570
+
+Artifact-only source and Windows type compilation against root's production-poll1568/build-debug. No Linux execution or OTP compatibility result is claimed. Root owns integration, staging and CI.
+
+Stage as tools/Validation/Erlang.DescriptorPollVmValidation. Build Erlang.DescriptorPollVmValidation.csproj with -p:RuntimeReferenceDirectory=<real runtime output> and a distinct --output. Four actual runtime assemblies are referenced; no candidate service source or fake VM/provider is compiled into this observer. Friend assembly name is Erlang.AsyncMicrostateValidation.dll. RuntimeReferenceDirectory supports absolute or repository-relative paths.
+
+CLI: dotnet <output>/Erlang.AsyncMicrostateValidation.dll all <report.json>, or replace all with one of the seven exact case names. All cases run independently and preserve full original errors plus cleanup failures; exit0 requires every case to pass.
+
+Cases: eager-two-vms (actual eager poll0 unmanaged row/OS thread per real VM with distinct services/accounting/TIDs); dispose-isolation (first physically joins/closes wake FDs, second VM still runs an actual actor); halt-no-flush (real held actor makes physical quiescence pending while logical halt result already returns, then actor release and HaltQuiescence require poll physical join); initializer-no-host-dispose (real actor kills actual initializer, waits owned DescriptorPollRuntimeLifetime558.Completion and checks poll closed BEFORE the finally block calls host Dispose); fail-before-start; fail-before-accounting; fail-entered-before-ready.
+
+Creation tests use the real internal ProcessRuntime constructor and existing RuntimeWorkerCreationPolicy. Its existing constructor checkpoint captures the actual in-construction VM; no field is reflection-written and no constructor/body is replaced. Selected Poll/0 hook throws one preallocated sentinel. The real constructor must throw with that same sentinel identity; unrelated failures are rejected. BeforeStart requires a proven unstarted poll owner; actual worker entry failures require actual thread join. EnteredBeforeReady also reads the real actual-thread MSACC attachment and requires its actual record to become inactive during rollback. Proof is checked at constructor throw before any extra host Dispose.
+
+Existing WorkerLifecycleAccess.cs and WorkerLifecycleNames.cs are copied byte-for-byte and used for readonly field access plus actual normal/dirty worker joins, owned contexts and streams cleanup. These helpers are not amended to forgive failures. Runtime standard constructors and real process spawning/termination are used; no synthetic lifecycle acknowledgment or TCS substitute is introduced. The Halt test's own gate holds a genuine actor delegate and is always released before its physical join.
+
+The observer does not test original Erlang fd data APIs, blocking writes or whole MSACC contracts. Existing DescriptorIoCases/PortDescriptorCases remain root's separate original OTP regression source. The observer is Linux-only; successful Windows compilation establishes type compatibility only. Linux execution must retain owned process receipts, real runtime assembly hashes, exact production source identity and all cleanup errors.
